{"author":"did:key:z6Mkmz8SWiUshwDMszSqwzMngt7ScNmsEj7vZoFRLjpcZTm9","evaluation":{"digest":{"sha256":"261340dd7514d8f03e84ae2355e9b614e9f857e573dbf09cc11855b96bb2ac86"}},"instructions":"Return exactly ACCEPT or REJECT.","network.jinn.binary-judgment.item-sha256":"sha256:7875ac002ba3354d1972a30842f77b41ab44ec8e17fe6e5dd2c9a1503b2f20ed","outputs":[{"mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","name":"judge-response","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.jinn.binary-judgment.observation.v1+json","name":"judge-observation","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.inspect-ai.eval-log+json","name":"inspect-log","required":false}],"payload":{"candidateAnswer":"Three turtles","evidence":"[D8:3 | 6:44 pm on 17 April, 2022] Nate: Sounds fun! I probably also have loads of books I haven't read in years. Sounds like a blast from the past!\n[D28:23 | 5:54 pm on 9 November, 2022] Nate: That sounds incredible! Nature truly has a way of reminding us to appreciate the beauty around us, and moments like those really stay with you. These critters also make me appreciate life's little joys. And guess what? I got them a new friend!","itemId":"urn:uuid:dcced280-9f99-5cba-bfb2-f60da0cb4abc","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:b04ca339173644c1a0c3131b9d99a3513fef349f3ae9f660aaad75e8fafc8e3f","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"How many turtles does Nate have?","referenceAnswer":"Three","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"b04ca339173644c1a0c3131b9d99a3513fef349f3ae9f660aaad75e8fafc8e3f"}}]},"profile":{"digest":{"sha256":"ebb34d8362e2cc3135847a5ad6f3ee3d9c2d9922a2b827aa9dfcbaf440b22557"},"uri":"https://spec.jinn.network/task-profiles/binary-judgment/2.0"},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/profiles/task-execution/v1"}